            {"id":"23810aed-28","kind":"component","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"color-handle/anatomyReview","name":"anatomyReview","fields":[{"path":"anatomyReview.notes","before":"RSP ColorHandle.tsx:52-81 and gen2 color-handle.css:35-82 (rings/shadow are styling on one element); ring part removed; relationship file has no scope.part.","after":"A7 (2026-11-20). RSP ColorHandle.tsx:52-81 and gen2 color-handle.css:35-82 (rings and shadow are styling on one element); the sources draw the color over a checkerboard (opacity-checkerboard is a nested component, size m in RSP and SWC 1st-gen; gen2 uses S, gap bead). Owner decisions C7 (the loupe is a second top-level part, like picker menu-container) and C9 (option `color`). The loupe lives inside the handle component in all three sources but outside the circle. `channel` dropped: no source has it. The nested-component kind of opacity-checkerboard and color-loupe is described here because the anatomy `component` field and `presentWhen` are not built. Owner decision C8: the loupe is present through the option isOpen (Figma Show color loupe, SWC open), not the state down."}]}
